WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
Speaker 1: All right, a big news,&nbsp;
at least for now and by tomorrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:10.160
this may be different. The Joe Biden vaccine&nbsp;
so-called mandate, as it is known, is going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:18.000
frozen frozen thanks to the decision of&nbsp;
a panel of Republican appointed judges.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.120
Now what we call the vaccine mandate, which is why&nbsp;
I said so-called is the requirement through OSHA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.640
that companies with more than 100 employees either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.480
have their employees get vaccinated and prove that&nbsp;
they are vaccinated, or you just test them weekly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.440
for COVID. So it's not much of a mandate, but it's&nbsp;
a protocol requirement. Call it whatever you want.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:46.160
Remember that Fox News's protocol or requirement&nbsp;
or whatever is stricter than what Joe Biden has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:53.520
put in place via OSHA at FOX. You have to prove&nbsp;
your vaccination status or test daily and wear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.280
masks in certain situations. All right. Well, per&nbsp;
the Washington Post, a federal appeals court has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.880
suspended has frozen the Biden administration's&nbsp;
new vaccine requirement for private companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.760
The federal appeals court in New Orleans, one&nbsp;
of the most conservative appeals courts in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:15.840
the country, is giving the Biden administration&nbsp;
until later today to respond to a lawsuit filed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.120
by Republican led states and businesses. The&nbsp;
decision was issued by a panel of three judges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.160
all appointed by Republican presidents.&nbsp;
This is the U.S. Circuit Court, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:31.680
U.S. Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit. The&nbsp;
judges wrote that there was quote cause to believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:39.360
there are grave statutory and constitutional&nbsp;
issues with the mandate. They have stayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:48.320
the mandate while it is assessed further. What&nbsp;
started all of this was a lawsuit filed late last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.200
week just before the weekend by some Republicans,&nbsp;
including Louisiana Attorney General Jeff Landry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:01.200
Now it's really important. This is a temporary&nbsp;
freeze on Biden's quote mandate. It is not a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.120
ruling on the merits of the policy. They want&nbsp;
more time to look at it. It's important to recall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:14.640
that vaccination requirements at the state level,&nbsp;
at local levels, by schools, by private companies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:22.080
they have almost completely held up in court&nbsp;
so far. The Biden requirement is different in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.400
two ways. Number one, it's broader. And number&nbsp;
two, it's coming from the federal government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.440
so it is different. That doesn't mean it's&nbsp;
not going to ultimately stand. It is also not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.880
actually a mandate, since you can test out doesn't&nbsp;
apply to employees who work remotely or outdoors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:44.080
doesn't apply to people who physically&nbsp;
work where other people don't work or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:51.280
shop. And as we talked about last week, these&nbsp;
requirements do work to get people vaccinated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.720
Very much so you can argue that it should be&nbsp;
against the law. You can argue that it's immoral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.760
but it works and it works really, really&nbsp;
well. When we look at companies ranging from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.760
United Airlines to the New York Police Department&nbsp;
to all sorts of companies, including ones where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.480
people were claiming I will, I'm not going to do&nbsp;
it, I'm not going to do it. It works very well now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.840
going back to the politics. This ruling was signed&nbsp;
by judges. One judge was a Reagan appointee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:23.680
just Judge Edith Jones and then Kyle. Kyle Duncan&nbsp;
and Kurt Engelhardt both were appointed by Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:30.880
Trump. This was the New Orleans based 5th Circuit&nbsp;
Court, considered one of the most conservative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:37.120
appeals courts in the country. It is likely that&nbsp;
other circuit courts, even given the same case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.960
would find differently. It is likely that&nbsp;
such a decision would probably not be upheld&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.920
by the Supreme Court if it ever got to that point.&nbsp;
Although we have a little bit of a wacky Supreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:53.840
Court right now, and you never know. White House&nbsp;
Chief of Staff Ron Klain was asked, What do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.600
think is ultimately going to happen? He says&nbsp;
he's confident it will be upheld. Of course he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.280
would say that, but let's listen to his reasoning.
Speaker 3: I want to ask you before I let you go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.400
about the court ruling yesterday on the vaccine,&nbsp;
on the vaccine protocols that Austin is putting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.040
Out sort of the soft mandate. I don't want to call&nbsp;
it a hard mandate because of the testing option.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.080
There's a freeze. What does that mean for&nbsp;
the federal government's efforts? I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.480
do you stop preparing for January 4th&nbsp;
in the moment? How does this work?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:29.520
Well, I think what it means for the time being&nbsp;
is that the the effectiveness of that vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:35.440
requirement is is frozen. I think we'll certainly&nbsp;
be well litigated, though well before January 3rd.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.720
I'm not sure really has much practical effect in&nbsp;
the short run. Look, these vaccine requirements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.800
have been litigated up and down the courts all&nbsp;
over the country. State requirements, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.480
one in Maine and every single court before this&nbsp;
one ruled that they were valid. The Supreme Court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:56.560
has turned back several times already various&nbsp;
efforts to enjoin other vaccine requirements.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.880
I'm quite confident that when this finally gets&nbsp;
fully adjudicated, not just a temporary order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:07.360
The validity of this requirement will be upheld.&nbsp;
It's common sense, chuck, if OSHA can tell people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:12.880
to wear a hard, hard hat on the job, right? Be&nbsp;
careful on chemicals. It can be put in place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.680
these simple measures to keep our workers safe.
Speaker 1: So of course, you would say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.440
with the Trump travel ban with with all&nbsp;
sorts of different things Trump did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.560
no matter what courts were doing, you always say,&nbsp;
I'm confident it will be upheld until there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.520
actually a decision otherwise. But I do think&nbsp;
Ron Klain is correct on this. That being said?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.840
There's a reasonable question, was this&nbsp;
requirement through OSHA, the best way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:43.520
to deal with anti-vaccine Republicans or had&nbsp;
is actually served to energize them further.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:49.040
I'm very interested in how the French have done&nbsp;
it. I have a family aunt, uncle cousins in France,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.440
and they came to me and they said, Sir,&nbsp;
because that's how my cousins talk to me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.880
They are very respectful of me. They said, You&nbsp;
know, here in France, we have a big anti-vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.680
problem. We have the distrust of government&nbsp;
people who are anti-vax, like in the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:08.480
and we have the distrust of big pharma people here&nbsp;
in France, like in the U.S. and you've got a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:15.280
of people here who believe homeopathy will treat&nbsp;
or cure or prevent COVID. You've got all of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:20.880
And if they had done a mandate in France, it&nbsp;
would have been absolute pandemonium. France took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.920
a different approach where they said, you don't&nbsp;
have to get a vaccine, but if you want to travel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.600
you want to go to a movie theater, you want to&nbsp;
go to a restaurant, you want to go to the great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:35.760
cafes where you get the salmon tartare and these&nbsp;
great dishes, which I love there. If you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:41.600
to do all of that stuff, you just are going to&nbsp;
either need to be presenting a negative test from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:47.920
I don't remember if it's twenty four, how many&nbsp;
hours every single time or you get vaccinated. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:54.560
the brilliance of it was it diffused the narrative&nbsp;
of a mandate, but it was like, this is something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.560 --> 00:07:01.120
really annoying. And so you had some people&nbsp;
from all walks of the anti-vaccine world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:08.080
saying, I'm not, I'm not for the vaccine, but&nbsp;
I just want to do something. There's a specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.680
thing I want to do. It's not about just being able&nbsp;
to go to work. So I'm going to go and I'm going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.520
to go and get vaccinated. I don't want to have&nbsp;
to test all the time. I want every time I want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:21.280
to go to a restaurant or whatever the case may&nbsp;
be. So I'm wondering aloud, is that an approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:26.880
that could have been maybe more effective? But&nbsp;
then you have the question of is that something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:33.360
Biden could really even do? Or does it have to&nbsp;
be done at the state or local level? Our system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:40.080
is different than that, which which is the case in&nbsp;
France. So be curious to hear from you about that

